# SvelteKit Rules — GoodEpoch Cursor Rules Pack v1
# Applies to: SvelteKit 2.x with Svelte 5
# Stack: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes), TypeScript 5.5+

## Svelte 5 Runes — The New Reactivity Model

- Svelte 5 uses runes (compiler directives) for all reactivity — not magical `$:` syntax
- `$state()` replaces `let` for reactive state
- `$derived()` replaces `$:` for derived values
- `$effect()` replaces `onMount`/`afterUpdate` for side effects
- `$props()` replaces `export let` for component props:
  ```svelte
  <script lang="ts">
    // Svelte 5 runes syntax
    let { name, onClose }: { name: string; onClose: () => void } = $props()
    let count = $state(0)
    let doubled = $derived(count * 2)
    
    $effect(() => {
      document.title = `Count: ${count}`
      return () => { document.title = 'App' } // cleanup
    })
  </script>
  
  <button onclick={() => count++}>{count} × 2 = {doubled}</button>
  ```

## SvelteKit File Conventions

```
src/
  routes/
    +page.svelte          # Page component
    +page.ts              # Universal load function
    +page.server.ts       # Server-only load + actions
    +layout.svelte        # Layout component
    +layout.server.ts     # Layout server load
    +error.svelte         # Error page
    +server.ts            # API endpoint (GET/POST/etc)
    (group)/              # Route group (no URL effect)
    [slug]/               # Dynamic route
```

## Load Functions

- Universal load (`+page.ts`): runs on server (SSR) AND client (navigation):
  ```typescript
  // +page.ts
  import type { PageLoad } from './$types'
  
  export const load: PageLoad = async ({ fetch, params }) => {
    const post = await fetch(`/api/posts/${params.slug}`).then(r => r.json())
    return { post }  // typed in +page.svelte via PageData
  }
  ```
- Server load (`+page.server.ts`): runs only on server, can access DB/secrets:
  ```typescript
  // +page.server.ts
  import type { PageServerLoad } from './$types'
  
  export const load: PageServerLoad = async ({ locals, params }) => {
    if (!locals.user) redirect(303, '/login')
    const user = await db.query.users.findFirst({ where: eq(users.id, locals.user.id) })
    return { user }
  }
  ```
- Always use `$types` — SvelteKit generates them automatically

## Form Actions (Mutations)

```typescript
// +page.server.ts
import { fail, redirect } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { Actions } from './$types'

export const actions = {
  createPost: async ({ request, locals }) => {
    if (!locals.user) redirect(303, '/login')
    
    const data = await request.formData()
    const result = createPostSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(data))
    
    if (!result.success) {
      return fail(400, { errors: result.error.flatten() })
    }
    
    await db.insert(posts).values({ ...result.data, userId: locals.user.id })
    redirect(303, '/posts')
  }
}
```

```svelte
<!-- +page.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import { enhance } from '$app/forms'
  let { form } = $props()  // ActionData from $types
</script>

<form method="POST" action="?/createPost" use:enhance>
  <input name="title" />
  {#if form?.errors?.fieldErrors.title}
    <p>{form.errors.fieldErrors.title}</p>
  {/if}
  <button>Create</button>
</form>
```

## Authentication with `locals`

- `locals` is the server-side request context — add user here in hooks:
  ```typescript
  // src/hooks.server.ts
  export const handle: Handle = async ({ event, resolve }) => {
    const session = event.cookies.get('session')
    if (session) {
      event.locals.user = await validateSession(session)
    }
    return resolve(event)
  }
  ```
- Declare locals type in `app.d.ts`:
  ```typescript
  declare global {
    namespace App {
      interface Locals { user: User | null }
      interface PageData {}
      interface Error { message: string; code?: string }
    }
  }
  ```

## Stores and State

- Svelte 5: use `$state` in `.svelte.ts` files for shared reactive state (not writable stores)
- `page` store from `$app/stores` for current URL, params, data
- URL state via `goto` with `replaceState` for filter state

## API Endpoints

```typescript
// src/routes/api/posts/+server.ts
import { json } from '@sveltejs/kit'
import type { RequestHandler } from './$types'

export const GET: RequestHandler = async ({ url, locals }) => {
  const limit = Number(url.searchParams.get('limit') ?? '20')
  const posts = await db.query.posts.findMany({ limit })
  return json(posts)
}
```

## Performance

- SvelteKit preloads linked pages on hover by default (`data-sveltekit-preload-data`)
- Disable for external links: `data-sveltekit-preload-data="off"`
- Static adapter for pure static sites; Cloudflare/Vercel adapters for SSR
- Images: `@sveltejs/enhanced-img` for automatic optimization
